[b][size=4]What it adds[/size][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Its own control[/b] - Flashlight, on [b]L[/b] by default and rebindable in Options > Controls like any other key. It is named in every language the game ships.[/*]
[*][b]A light[/b] - the engine's own spot light, the kind the vehicles' headlights use.[/*]
[*][b]Guards see it[/b] - at night a guard looking your way sees the light from up to 60 m, and one you shine it on notices you even with his back turned.[/*]
[*][b]A click[/b] - refurbished from an unused in-game sound.[/*]
[*][b]A HUD [/b]- above the diamond counter, showing whether the light is on or off.[/*]
[/list]
[b][size=4]Settings[/size][/b]
In the [b]Mod Configuration[/b] menu:
[list]
[*][b]Cone[/b] - small, medium or large beam. Medium by default.[/*]
[*][b]Shadows[/b] - whether the light casts shadows. On by default.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/farcry2/mods/368]FCSE[/url] 1.3.0 or later, the plugin loader this runs in. Far Cry 2 1.03, Steam or GOG.[/*]
[/list]
[b][size=4]Installing[/size][/b]
The download is a JackAll layer, which both installers read as-is:
[list]
[*][b]Vortex[/b] - with the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/site/mods/2143]Far Cry 2 extension[/url] installed, drop the zip in and enable it.[/*]
[*][b]JackAll[/b] - add the zip in [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/farcry2/mods/370]JackAll[/url].[/*]
[/list]
If you're stuck, [url=https://jbebe.github.io/farcry-sdk/jackall/installing-mods/]here's a detailed instruction[/url].

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Mods that change the controls[/b] (inputactionmapcommon.xml or defaultusercontrols.xml) conflict. Whichever loads last wins; if the other mod wins, there is no Flashlight control.[/*]
[*][b]Mods that replace the HUD[/b] (hud.mgb) conflict the same way. If the other mod wins, the flashlight works without its icon.[/*]
[/list]
